# The requirement written at the point of use (the book, assignment and declaration sites): a reached declaration of
# an existing place keeps the type check, the evaluation of its right side and the assignment. C is an ordinary
# Structure nested in D and is launched as D\C() over D. D declares int: x 0; the body first writes the observable
# marker data\entered := 1, then `int: x tick()`, then carries the local's value into the data. The pair is
# compatible: entered 1, tick 1, x 7. The marker and the last write are explicit paths: a bare-name assignment to an
# input place of the called Structure writes the place of the activation, not the graph.
int: ticks 0
fn: tick () int
    node\ticks := node\ticks + 1
    return: 7
@: D (
    int: entered 0
    int: x 0
    C(data\entered := 1; int: x tick(); data\x := x)
)
D\C()
